  "body": "A native job can select an existing quality with the same generic name and different parameters. The controller formal check passes.\n\nA synthetic 40 mm steel job requested Cobra Cut D 0.25 and Ra 0.30 using the name QN2. The control displayed Ra 0.70 and made three cuts. On the same setup, a new quality name with the identical 0.30 tuple displayed Ra 0.30 and made four cuts. A separate new name requesting 0.70 displayed 0.70 and made three cuts. The 20 mm Berco baseline also displayed an existing QN2 at 0.70 for a 0.30 request.\n\nBind each native work to the intended quality with a name that identifies its settings. The result must be independent of the job name and the order of works. Cover a preexisting quality and a repeated import of the same program. Check both the effective values in the control editor and the measured pass offsets. Update rough clearance and any public condition claim that relies on the prior binding. Refuse unqualified combinations before writing a bundle.\n\nThe name affects pass count and actual wire offsets. The same nominal input can give a different cut.\n\nSuggested labels are P1, effort:high, area:post, bug and source:agent.\n",
